I'll search for the current best practices to change a `<span>` color on mouseover using HTML/CSS.

Based on my search, here are several ways to change a `<span>` color on mouseover, from simplest to more advanced:

## 1. Pure CSS :hover (Recommended - No JavaScript needed)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
  .hover-span {
    color: black;           /* Default color */
    transition: color 0.3s; /* Smooth color transition */
  }

  .hover-span:hover {
    color: red;             /* Color on mouseover */
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <span class="hover-span">Hover over me!</span>
</body>
</html>
```

## 2. Inline Style (Not Recommended, but works for quick tests)

```html
<span onmouseover="this.style.color='red'" onmouseout="this.style.color='black'">
  Hover over me!
</span>
```

## 3. JavaScript with Event Listeners (For dynamic/complex behavior)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
  #mySpan {
    color: black;
    transition: color 0.3s ease;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <span id="mySpan">Hover over me!</span>

<script>
  const span = document.getElementById('mySpan');

  span.addEventListener('mouseover', function() {
    this.style.color = 'red';
  });

  span.addEventListener('mouseout', function() {
    this.style.color = 'black';
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

## 4. CSS Classes with JavaScript (Best for maintainability)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
  .highlight {
    color: red;
  }

  .default {
    color: black;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <span id="mySpan" class="default">Hover over me!</span>

<script>
  const span = document.getElementById('mySpan');

  span.addEventListener('mouseover', () => {
    span.classList.remove('default');
    span.classList.add('highlight');
  });

  span.addEventListener('mouseout', () => {
    span.classList.remove('highlight');
    span.classList.add('default');
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

## 5. Modern JavaScript with toggle (Cleaner)

```javascript
const span = document.getElementById('mySpan');

span.addEventListener('mouseenter', () => span.classList.add('highlight'));
span.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => span.classList.remove('highlight'));
```

---

## Recommendation

| Approach | When to Use |
|----------|-------------|
| **CSS `:hover`** | Simple color changes — **preferred method** |
| **JavaScript classes** | Need to change multiple properties or trigger other logic |
| **Inline handlers** | Quick prototyping only (avoid in production) |

The **CSS `:hover` approach (#1)** is best for simple color changes because:
- No JavaScript required
- Better performance
- Cleaner separation of concerns
- Works even with JavaScript disabled

Sources:
1. https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/:hover
2. https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/mouseover_event
3. https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/transition
4. https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/EventTarget/addEventListener

